A||||14||HAGS||Its all over...||||1||
Z||000000||HAGS||02-03-2001||08:16 AM||||I can almost guarantee something broke in the engine....I was only doing 70 or so... huge explosion/smoke, no visible damage from looking at the external...its sitting at the gas station I was able to coast to...I was just thinking to myself it was running the best it has since I had got it...wham!  <BR>Im a little poor boy, just get a new Fiero or look for a 2.8 from someone thats upgrading?  <BR>My car sucks hardcore so I probably wont be swapping, but since I bought all the crap to work on the internal I will probably remove the engine and see what I can do with it after I get my friend to tow it back to San Antonio for me.<BR>I've been looking at a few Formula's from some members but no way a bank is gonna give me a loan...I have no credit, cant even get a credit card without paying $100 anuall fee...the dealer my mom works at even rejected me for a 12k ZX2...||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||02-03-2001||10:57 PM||||Oh man, not what we wanted to hear!  Broken connecting rod?  Messed up crankshaft?  Best thing to do is tear it down and see if it is worth saving at all, if not try to part it out or sell it as a good frame for a kit, then you'll have a little money to try and get a good one, hopefully.<P>Hope everything works out ok!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||02-04-2001||03:26 PM||||Is it possible the ignition module or coil broke down and died a slow death? Possibly the muffler filled with gas vapor, the engine tried to fire and lit off all the fumes, then died. If there's no oil or mangled metal, I'd check there, first. Check the gray connector on top of the coil, too. Mine used to work loose and break the connection.<BR>Good luck. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
