Z||000008||HAGS||02-05-2001||12:55 PM||||I killed myself riding my bike up to that dealer, spent three hours their either test driving the Fiero or cashing bonds so I could buy it...well I'd say the Fiero was worth $600, as we were almost done with the paperwork he decides to tell me the $695 on the window is just the downpayment, all the cars on the lot are $4000....no car on that lot was worth $4000 but I'd have to say all of them were decent prices if you were just paying the down payment...  I walked out of there screaming my head off saying that the Blue Book value for his Fiero was only $500 and I'd be sure never to let my friends go near the lot.<BR>Oh yeah, also said I'd rather buy a Mint 88GT with T-Tops for $4000<P>The car was an 86 regular coupe, 4 cylinder 5-speed... maybe I should offer him my blown 86 Sport Coupe for 2k!!||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||02-05-2001||02:53 PM||||I do work for some of those kind of dealers. Usually one of those buy here-pay heres. What they do is get what they have in it or almost anyway, for a down payment. Then there profit is when people make the payments. Thats what protects them from low lifes who buy and make them repo it. I remember one car in particular, a Buick convertible, they sold and repod at least 5 times. They made a few thousand and still owned the car. Hope you find out it was really something minor like coil or module.<BR>BTW, any of you from around Columbus has heard of PayDays Used cars. Their owned by Richart Ford. Hes made millions selling the cars he wouldnt put on his own used car lot, selling them just like that.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Pontiaddict||02-06-2001||12:19 AM||||Reminds me of something that happened to me. When I had my '84, I was driving over to a friends house, when all of the sudden it dies. It was running the best that it had run since I owned it, and I figured that I blew it up. So I walk half a mile in the dark to my friends house to call my parents to bring the tow chain. We decided to go back and take a look at the car while my parents were coming. It turned out that the coil wire had worked it's way loose and the excess gap it was getting until it fell off was why my car was running so good. I stuck the wire back on and it fired back up. They really need a light in the engine compartment.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  You might just luck out.||||reg||1
Z||000011||HAGS||02-06-2001||08:14 AM||||Didnt sound like it gave out, sounded like it blew up and something was being thrown around inside it.||||reg||1
Z||000012||DavidHenshaw||02-06-2001||02:12 PM||||Garrison is right on the Buy Here Pay Here thing. There was a V6 fiero at one of those places here in town and they wanted $3,995 for a very average car. I bought one in about the same shape from an individual for $1,500. I don't know who these people think they are kidding. The 4K fiero sat on their lot forever.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
